            <ArticleTitle>[Nutritional follow-up after bariatric surgery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>51-54</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0038-0814(16)30215-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.soin.2016.10.012</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lifelong monitoring after weight loss surgery is recommended in order to check the efficacy of the procedure and to identify complications. Particular attention must be paid to the nutritional status of pregnant women and in the event of surgical complications. Education programmes must be offered at every stage of the care pathway in order to favour the compliance required for the follow-up.</AbstractText>
